# A chain: gizmo requires libgadget, libgadget requires libwidget, and
# libwidget — the headline — breaks. The runner skips libgadget for
# libwidget, and then skips gizmo for libgadget: each member's
# requires.<i> names the member it actually declares, so each skip
# names its own prerequisite and not the root of the chain. The log
# holds one section, libwidget's, and the record holds three words.
#
# The sentences differ down the chain, and deliberately. libgadget is
# told libwidget fails to build, which is what happened to libwidget.
# gizmo is told libgadget could not be built — not that it fails to
# build, because libgadget failed at nothing; it was skipped — and a
# reader who follows the blame from gizmo to libgadget to libwidget
# finds a true sentence at every step.
# SYNTHESIZED from the cohort runner in internal/verify/tart/tart.go,
# not captured: see README.md.
members: libwidget libgadget gizmo
outcome: failed
libwidget.state: failed
libwidget.detail: Failed to build libwidget: command execution failed
libwidget.reported: failed
libgadget.state: blocked
libgadget.blamed: libwidget
libgadget.detail: libwidget fails to build; this member is untested
libgadget.reported: skipped libwidget
gizmo.state: blocked
gizmo.blamed: libgadget
gizmo.detail: libgadget could not be built, so this member was not built; it is untested
